eck what other tenants are consuming).\n\n\"The documented rate limit represents the total shared capacity across all tenants on the vendor's platform, and the actual per-client enforceable limit is a dynamically allocated fraction of that total divided among active consumers \u2014 falsifiable by measuring the per-client rate limit during low-traffic hours (minimal contention) and comparing it to the documented limit, then repeating during high-traffic hours and observing whether the per-client limit decreases proportionally.\"\n\nThis is different from both previous hypotheses. It explains the discrepancy, it's testable, and it predicts that the per-client limit should vary based on other tenants' activity.\n\nLet me refine it to be concise and sharp.", "time": {"start": 1788444664410, "end": 1788444668037}, "id": "prt_0679be25a001LCVBVDHB5Tzb1l", "sessionID": "ses_fc05b5faaffe6AOkpATeDYR5P3", "messageID": "msg_0679bdb9e001ooItTZr4V1ll23"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The documented rate limit represents the total shared capacity across all tenants on the vendor's platform rather than a dedicated per-client allocation, and the actual enforceable per-client limit is a dynamically shrinking fraction of that total divided among active consumers \u2014 falsifiable by measuring the per-client rate limit during low-contention hours and comparing it to the documented figure, then repeating during high-contention hours and observing whether the per-client limit decreases proportionally to concurrent tenant activity.", "time": {"start": 1788444668051, "end": 1788444668958}, "id": "prt_0679bf093001ZyBbyKBCpNt6Fm", "sessionID": "ses_fc05b5faaffe6AOkpATeDYR5P3", "messageID": "msg_0679bdb9e001ooItTZr4V1ll23"}, {"reason": "stop", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 42137, "input": 162, "output": 0, "reasoning": 498, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 41503}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_0679bf42c001Fu2eCuHx9O5SXx", "sessionID": "ses_fc05b5faaffe6AOkpATeDYR5P3", "messageID": "msg_0679